  note      = {[READ] Quantifies Arctic amplification feedback budget; surface albedo only ~1/3 of total.},
  annote    = {Decomposes Arctic amplification (2x global warming) into feedback components using CMIP5 ensemble. Key finding: surface albedo contributes only ~35%; dominant factors are lapse-rate feedback (~45%), Planck feedback, cloud/water vapor. Lapse-rate feedback linked to stable BL structure—strong inversions trap warming near surface. Implies SBL mixing biases directly affect amplification magnitude. High-impact paper (>1000 citations); critical for linking our BL work to climate relevance.}
}

