  annote    = {Hierarchy of turbulence closures (Levels 2, 2.5, 3, 4) based on TKE budget. Level 2.5 (prognostic TKE + diagnostic length scale) operationally popular. Advantages: physical TKE transport, self-consistent stability dependence. Disadvantages: added PDE, sensitive to length-scale formulation, still has grid-dependence issues. Our curvature correction orthogonal—could be applied to M-Y mixing length or stability functions. Many NWP models use M-Y variants (NCEP, Navy).}
}

@techreport{Janjic2001NCEP,
